contentText:
Hilary Duff is joined by her son Luca in her studio to discuss her new album Luck.. or Something , her historic career and their household dynamic for Billboard Family.

Hilary Duff: Are you not gonna say anything about what I&#8217;m wearing?

Luca: It&#8217;s just not&#8230; It&#8217;s not it.&nbsp;

Hilary Duff: What?&nbsp;

Luca: Arsenal it&#8217;s not it.&nbsp;

Hilary Duff: What are you wearing?&nbsp;

Luca: Real Madrid. I&#8217;m not a fan of them, by the way. No.&nbsp;

Hilary Duff: You don&#8217;t want to give anybody the wrong idea.&nbsp;

Luca: No.

Hilary Duff: I&#8217;m wearing a soccer jersey.&nbsp;

Luca: Yeah, but, like, at least, like, make it a Man City jersey. That&#8217;s Arsenal&#8217;s, trash.&nbsp;

Hilary Duff: I didn&#8217;t sit and sew this, but I did think you were going to be excited by it, and you&#8217;re like&#8230;&nbsp;

Luca: It&#8217;s just not it. Hi, I&#8217;m Luca, and today I&#8217;m interviewing my mom for Billboard Family. Hi, mom.&nbsp;

Hilary Duff: Hi, Luca!&nbsp;

Luca: You&#8217;re releasing a new album, Luck&#8230; or Something . When did you start making this song?

Hilary Duff: I think it was about just over a year ago when the first like ideas were kind of starting to take shape. You probably remember being in the kitchen and, like, hearing stuff on our phones that was like the first kind of like initial sounds that we were, like, toying with. Remember?

Luca: Yeah, I think so.&nbsp;

Hilary Duff: I think it was like over a year ago.

Luca: How did you choose the album title?

Hilary Duff: I just want to let all the listeners know that in the car, I asked Luca if he knew the title of my album. And he didn&#8217;t. Okay. So it goes to show you, I would play you guys songs in the car on the way to school, but like, you don&#8217;t know the title of my new album, which is&#8230;&nbsp;

Luca: You just never told me it. You didn&#8217;t.&nbsp;

Hilary Duff: Fine.&nbsp;

Luca: It&#8217;s just what it is.

Hilary Duff: Facts.

Keep watching for more!
